      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-30T16:31:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This feels like there is a better way. The instructions are just a linked list. So, can we just assign the `instructions_` over to the new block and clear out the initial one. If you did the `Exits` replacement afterwards then it should remove the incorrect parent pointer as the exit switches are gone.",
      "revId": "7c3b14104f48ccf234353763cead072a03e28a8b",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
